    "title": "<p>International Cowden Consortium (ICC) and National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) operational criteria for Cowden syndrome without known family history of <em>PTEN</em> mutation</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Charles G. Eberhart",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"605\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Pathognomonic criteria:</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Adult dysplastic cerebellar gangliocytoma (cerebellar tumours)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Mucocutaneous lesions<sup>a</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 70.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 36.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 70.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"49\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 416.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 70.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"556\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Facial trichilemmomas, any number<sup>a</sup> (at least two biopsy-proven trichilemmomas<sup>b</sup>)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Acral keratoses</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Papillomatous papules</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Mucosal lesions&nbsp;(especially hamartomatous gastrointestinal polyps)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Autism spectrum disorder and macrocephaly<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em><span style=\"color: black;\">Major criteria:</span></em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Breast cancer</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Thyroid cancer (non-medullary)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Macrocephaly (megalocephaly; i.e. 97th percentile and above)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Endometrial cancer</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Mucocutaneous lesions<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 62.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 36.8pt; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 62.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"49\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 416.8pt; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 62.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"556\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">One biopsy-proven trichilemmoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Multiple palmoplantar keratoses</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Multifocal cutaneous facial papules</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.5pt; text-indent: -14.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Macular pigmentation of the glans penis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Multiple gastrointestinal hamartomas or ganglioneuromas<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>ICC criteria only, <sup>b</sup>NCCN 2010 criteria only (modified from <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{21194675}</span>).</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Note: In 1996, the ICC <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{8673088}</span> compiled operational diagnostic criteria for Cowden syndrome on the basis of the published literature and their own clinical experience <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26142096; 17167516}</span>. NCCN has also established a set of operational clinical diagnostic criteria for identifying individuals with possible Cowden syndrome <span class=\"Ref-misc\">[[National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN). NCCN clinical practice guidelines in oncology (NCCN guidelines): genetic/familial high-risk assessment: breast and ovarian cancer. Version 1.2010. Fort Washington (PA): NCCN; 2010. Available from: https://www.nccn.org/professionals/physician_gls/default.aspx.]]</span>.</p>",
